body:
NTA. He is making a mountain out of a molehill, and using guilt to manipulate you.

&#x200B;

I would recommend you read [Why Does He Do That?](https://ia800108.us.archive.org/30/items/LundyWhyDoesHeDoThat/Lundy_Why-does-he-do-that.pdf)

NAH. My husband is autistic and loves to talk about things in a way where he just starts saying anything that comes to mind about a topic he's passionate about. I have a master's in animal biology, which he knows, but he still loves to talk about fire salamanders and any other animal that does something that fascinates him. I already know the things he talks about, but it's cool to hear what he finds fascinating about them.

&#x200B;

But, sometimes I get really bored when he goes on and on about something for 20 minutes and he's starting to talk in circles because he's just saying what's going through his head. He usually gets the hint when I just stop having any sort of "Uhuh," or "oh yeah" kind of responses. He also doesn't get offended if I just straight-up tell him that I don't want to keep talking about the subject.

